    "quote": "Let $\\inst$ be an instance of \\bestarm{} consisting of one arm with mean $\\mu$ and $n$ arms with means on $[\\mu - \\Delta,\\mu)$. There exist universal constants $\\delta$ and $c$ (independent of $n$ and $\\Delta$) such that for any algorithm $\\alg$ that correctly solves $\\inst$ with probability $1-\\delta$, the expected number of samples drawn from the optimal arm is at least $c\\Delta^{-2}\\ln n$."
